{"id":"mahabharata-5-029","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":29,"title":"एकोनत्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 29 · Krishna's answer to Sanjaya","summary":{"en":"Krishna tells Sanjaya that he desires the Pandavas' welfare and the Kurus' peace alike, but that action, not withdrawal, is the way of the world and of the gods; for a Kshatriya to fight for his rights is dharma. He recalls the outrage done to Draupadi, says the Pandavas are ready for peace or war, and warns that Dhritarashtra's sons are a forest of which the Pandavas are the tigers.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವರ ಹಿತವನ್ನೂ ಕುರುಗಳ ಶಾಂತಿಯನ್ನೂ ಸಮನಾಗಿ ಬಯಸುವೆ, ಆದರೆ ನಿವೃತ್ತಿಯಲ್ಲ ಕರ್ಮವೇ ಲೋಕದ ಮತ್ತು ದೇವತೆಗಳ ಮಾರ್ಗ, ಹಕ್ಕಿಗಾಗಿ ಹೋರಾಡುವುದು ಕ್ಷತ್ರಿಯನ ಧರ್ಮ ಎಂದು ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ಸಂಜಯನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದ್ರೌಪದಿಗಾದ ಅವಮಾನವನ್ನು ನೆನೆದು, ಪಾಂಡವರು ಶಾಂತಿಗೂ ಯುದ್ಧಕ್ಕೂ ಸಿದ್ಧರು ಎಂದು ಹೇಳಿ, ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರಪುತ್ರರು ಕಾಡು, ಪಾಂಡವರು ಅದರ ಹುಲಿಗಳು ಎಂದು ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"श्रीकृष्ण सञ्जय से कहते हैं कि वे पाण्डवों का हित और कुरुओं की शान्ति समान रूप से चाहते हैं, पर कर्म ही, निवृत्ति नहीं, संसार और देवताओं का मार्ग है; क्षत्रिय के लिए अपने अधिकार के लिए लड़ना धर्म है। वे द्रौपदी के अपमान को याद करते हैं, कहते हैं कि पाण्डव शान्ति या युद्ध दोनों के लिए तैयार हैं, और चेताते हैं कि धृतराष्ट्र के पुत्र वन हैं जिसके बाघ पाण्डव हैं।","te":"పాండవుల హితాన్ని, కురువుల శాంతిని సమానంగా కోరుకుంటానని, కానీ నివృత్తి కాదు కర్మే లోకానికీ దేవతలకూ మార్గమని, హక్కు కోసం పోరాడడం క్షత్రియ ధర్మమని శ్రీకృష్ణుడు సంజయునికి చెబుతాడు. ద్రౌపదికి జరిగిన అవమానాన్ని గుర్తుచేసి, పాండవులు శాంతికీ యుద్ధానికీ సిద్ధమని, ధృతరాష్ట్రపుత్రులు అడవి అయితే పాండవులు దాని పులులని హెచ్చరిస్తాడు.","ta":"பாண்டவர்களின் நலனையும் குருக்களின் அமைதியையும் சமமாக விரும்புகிறேன், ஆனால் விலகல் அல்ல செயலே உலகுக்கும் தேவர்களுக்கும் வழி, உரிமைக்காகப் போரிடுவது க்ஷத்ரியனுக்கு அறம் என்று ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் ஸஞ்ஜயனிடம் சொல்கிறார். திரௌபதிக்கு நேர்ந்த அவமானத்தை நினைவுகூர்ந்து, பாண்டவர்கள் அமைதிக்கும் போருக்கும் தயார் என்று சொல்லி, த்ருதராஷ்டிர மைந்தர்கள் காடு, பாண்டவர்கள் அதன் புலிகள் என்று எச்சரிக்கிறார்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവരുടെ ക്ഷേമവും കൗരവരുടെ സമാധാനവും ഒരുപോലെ ആഗ്രഹിക്കുന്നുവെന്ന് കൃഷ്ണൻ സഞ്ജയനോട് പറയുന്നു; എന്നാൽ ലോകത്തിന്റെയും ദേവന്മാരുടെയും വഴി പിന്മാറ്റമല്ല, പ്രവർത്തനമാണെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. ക്ഷത്രിയൻ തന്റെ അവകാശത്തിനായി പൊരുതുന്നത് ധർമ്മമാണ്. ദ്രൗപദിയോട് ചെയ്ത അപമാനം അദ്ദേഹം ഓർമ്മിപ്പിക്കുന്നു; സമാധാനത്തിനോ യുദ്ധത്തിനോ പാണ്ഡവർ തയ്യാറാണെന്നും, ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രപുത്രന്മാർ ഒരു കാടാണെന്നും പാണ്ഡവർ അതിലെ കടുവകളാണെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം മുന്നറിയിപ്പ് നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.29; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"संजययानपर्व","titleEn":"Sanjayayana Parva (Sanjaya's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अविनाशं संजय पाण्डवाना-\nमिच्छाम्यहं भूतिमेषां प्रियं च ।\nतथा राज्ञो धृतराष्ट्रस्य सूत\nसदाशंसे बहुपुत्रस्य वृद्धिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wish the Pandavas' safety, Sanjaya, and their prosperity and pleasure; and likewise, charioteer, I always wish growth for King Dhritarashtra, father of many sons."}},{"n":2,"text":"कामो हि मे संजय नित्यमेव\nनान्यद्ब्रूयां तान्प्रति शाम्यतेति ।\nराज्ञश्च हि प्रियमेतच्छृणोमि\nमन्ये चैतत्पाण्डवानां समर्थम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For it is always my wish, Sanjaya, and I would not say anything else to them than: be peaceful. I hear that this is the king's wish, and I think this is the right course for the Pandavas."}},{"n":3,"text":"सुदुष्करश्चात्र शमो हि नूनं\nप्रदर्शितः संजय पाण्डवेन ।\nयस्मिन्गृद्धो धृतराष्ट्रः सपुत्रः\nकस्मादेषां कलहो नात्र मूर्च्छेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely, Sanjaya, the Pandava has shown peace to be very hard; for Dhritarashtra with his sons is greedy, so why should this quarrel not swell here?"}},{"n":4,"text":"तत्त्वं धर्मं विचरन्संजयेह\nमत्तश्च जानासि युधिष्ठिराच्च ।\nअथो कस्मात्संजय पाण्डवस्य\nउत्साहिनः पूरयतः स्वकर्म ।\nयथाख्यातमावसतः कुटुम्बं\nपुराकल्पात्साधु विलोपमात्थ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Practicing dharma truly, Sanjaya, you know it from me and from Yudhishthira. Then why, Sanjaya, do you blame the Pandava, who is energetic, who fulfills his duty and who lives supporting his household as described, as if he were neglecting it from olden times?"}},{"n":5,"text":"अस्मिन्विधौ वर्तमाने यथाव-\nदुच्चावचा मतयो ब्राह्मणानाम् ।\nकर्मणाहुः सिद्धिमेके परत्र\nहित्वा कर्म विद्यया सिद्धिमेके ।\nनाभुञ्जानो भक्ष्यभोज्यस्य तृप्ये-\nद्विद्वानपीह विदितं ब्राह्मणानाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this rule as it stands, the opinions of the Brahmins are varied: some say that success in the other world comes by action; some, leaving action, say success comes by knowledge. Yet even a learned man here is not satisfied without eating food, as is known among Brahmins."}},{"n":6,"text":"या वै विद्याः साधयन्तीह कर्म\nतासां फलं विद्यते नेतरासाम् ।\nतत्रेह वै दृष्टफलं तु कर्म\nपीत्वोदकं शाम्यति तृष्णयार्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of those sciences that bring about action here, the fruit is seen; not of the others. There action has visible fruit: a person tormented by thirst is calmed by drinking water."}},{"n":7,"text":"सोऽयं विधिर्विहितः कर्मणैव\nतद्वर्तते संजय तत्र कर्म ।\nतत्र योऽन्यत्कर्मणः साधु मन्ये-\nन्मोघं तस्य लपितं दुर्बलस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"This rule is set by action alone, and action goes on, Sanjaya, there; whoever there thinks other than action good, the speech of that weak person is in vain."}},{"n":8,"text":"कर्मणामी भान्ति देवाः परत्र\nकर्मणैवेह प्लवते मातरिश्वा ।\nअहोरात्रे विदधत्कर्मणैव\nअतन्द्रितो नित्यमुदेति सूर्यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By action these gods shine in the other world; by action the wind blows here; by action, ordering day and night, the sun always rises untiringly."}},{"n":9,"text":"मासार्धमासानथ नक्षत्रयोगा-\nनतन्द्रितश्चन्द्रमा अभ्युपैति ।\nअतन्द्रितो दहते जातवेदाः\nसमिध्यमानः कर्म कुर्वन्प्रजाभ्यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Untiring, the moon passes through half-months, months and the conjunctions of stars; untiring, Fire burns, kindled, doing his work for the people."}},{"n":10,"text":"अतन्द्रिता भारमिमं महान्तं\nबिभर्ति देवी पृथिवी बलेन ।\nअतन्द्रिताः शीघ्रमपो वहन्ति\nसंतर्पयन्त्यः सर्वभूतानि नद्यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Untiring, the goddess Earth bears this great burden with her strength; untiring, the rivers carry water swiftly, satisfying all beings."}},{"n":11,"text":"अतन्द्रितो वर्षति भूरितेजाः\nसंनादयन्नन्तरिक्षं दिवं च ।\nअतन्द्रितो ब्रह्मचर्यं चचार\nश्रेष्ठत्वमिच्छन्बलभिद्देवतानाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Untiring, the greatly powerful rain-god rains, making the sky and heaven resound; untiring, the destroyer of Bala practiced chastity, wishing to be the best of the gods."}},{"n":12,"text":"हित्वा सुखं मनसश्च प्रियाणि\nतेन शक्रः कर्मणा श्रैष्ठ्यमाप ।\nसत्यं धर्मं पालयन्नप्रमत्तो\nदमं तितिक्षां समतां प्रियं च ।\nएतानि सर्वाण्युपसेवमानो\nदेवराज्यं मघवान्प्राप मुख्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Giving up pleasure and the mind's delights, Shakra by that action gained supremacy; guarding truth and dharma, heedful, cultivating self-control, patience, equanimity and kindness, Maghavan, serving all these, got the chief rule of the gods."}},{"n":13,"text":"बृहस्पतिर्ब्रह्मचर्यं चचार\nसमाहितः संशितात्मा यथावत् ।\nहित्वा सुखं प्रतिरुध्येन्द्रियाणि\nतेन देवानामगमद्गौरवं सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brihaspati practiced chastity, collected, with sharpened self, as is proper; giving up pleasure and restraining his senses, by that he gained eminence among the gods."}},{"n":14,"text":"नक्षत्राणि कर्मणामुत्र भान्ति\nरुद्रादित्या वसवोऽथापि विश्वे ।\nयमो राजा वैश्रवणः कुबेरो\nगन्धर्वयक्षाप्सरसश्च शुभ्राः ।\nब्रह्मचर्यं वेदविद्याः क्रियाश्च\nनिषेवमाणा मुनयोऽमुत्र भान्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The stars shine in the other world by action, and the Rudras, Adityas, Vasus and Vishvedevas, King Yama, Vaishravana Kubera, the Gandharvas, Yakshas and bright nymphs; and sages shine there by practicing chastity, Vedic knowledge and rites."}},{"n":15,"text":"जानन्निमं सर्वलोकस्य धर्मं\nब्राह्मणानां क्षत्रियाणां विशां च ।\nस कस्मात्त्वं जानतां ज्ञानवान्स-\nन्व्यायच्छसे संजय कौरवार्थे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing this dharma for the whole world, for Brahmins, Kshatriyas and Vaishyas, why, Sanjaya, being among the knowing and knowledgeable, do you exert yourself for the Kauravas' sake?"}},{"n":16,"text":"आम्नायेषु नित्यसंयोगमस्य\nतथाश्वमेधे राजसूये च विद्धि ।\nसंयुज्यते धनुषा वर्मणा च\nहस्तत्राणै रथशस्त्रैश्च भूयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know that he is always engaged in the scriptures, and in the Ashvamedha and Rajasuya; he is further joined with bow, armor, hand-guards, chariot and weapons."}},{"n":17,"text":"ते चेदिमे कौरवाणामुपाय-\nमधिगच्छेयुरवधेनैव पार्थाः ।\nधर्मत्राणं पुण्यमेषां कृतं स्या-\nदार्ये वृत्ते भीमसेनं निगृह्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"If these Parthas obtained a way against the Kauravas without killing, that would be a merit of protecting dharma, if by restraining Bhimasena they kept to the noble way."}},{"n":18,"text":"ते चेत्पित्र्ये कर्मणि वर्तमाना\nआपद्येरन्दिष्टवशेन मृत्युम् ।\nयथाशक्त्या पूरयन्तः स्वकर्म\nतदप्येषां निधनं स्यात्प्रशस्तम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If, though engaged in their father's duty, they met death by fate, while fulfilling their duty as best they could, even that death of theirs would be praised."}},{"n":19,"text":"उताहो त्वं मन्यसे सर्वमेव\nराज्ञां युद्धे वर्तते धर्मतन्त्रम् ।\nअयुद्धे वा वर्तते धर्मतन्त्रं\nतथैव ते वाचमिमां शृणोमि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or do you think that in every case the system of dharma for kings lies in war, or lies in non-war? I hear your speech just so."}},{"n":20,"text":"चातुर्वर्ण्यस्य प्रथमं विभाग-\nमवेक्ष्य त्वं संजय स्वं च कर्म ।\nनिशम्याथो पाण्डवानां स्वकर्म\nप्रशंस वा निन्द वा या मतिस्ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look at the first division of the four classes, Sanjaya, and your own duty; and having heard of the Pandavas' own duty, praise it or blame it, as you think."}},{"n":21,"text":"अधीयीत ब्राह्मणोऽथो यजेत\nदद्यादियात्तीर्थमुख्यानि चैव ।\nअध्यापयेद्याजयेच्चापि याज्या-\nन्प्रतिग्रहान्वा विदितान्प्रतीच्छेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A Brahmin should study, sacrifice, give and go to the chief holy places; he may teach, officiate for those who should have sacrifices performed, and accept known gifts."}},{"n":22,"text":"तथा राजन्यो रक्षणं वै प्रजानां\nकृत्वा धर्मेणाप्रमत्तोऽथ दत्त्वा ।\nयज्ञैरिष्ट्वा सर्ववेदानधीत्य\nदारान्कृत्वा पुण्यकृदावसेद्गृहान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise a Kshatriya, protecting the people by dharma, heedful, and giving, having sacrificed with offerings and studied all the Vedas, and taken a wife, should live in his house doing good deeds."}},{"n":23,"text":"वैश्योऽधीत्य कृषिगोरक्षपण्यै-\nर्वित्तं चिन्वन्पालयन्नप्रमत्तः ।\nप्रियं कुर्वन्ब्राह्मणक्षत्रियाणां\nधर्मशीलः पुण्यकृदावसेद्गृहान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A Vaishya, having studied, gathering wealth by farming, cattle-keeping and trade, and guarding it, heedful, pleasing the Brahmins and Kshatriyas, virtuous and doing good, should live in his house."}},{"n":24,"text":"परिचर्या वन्दनं ब्राह्मणानां\nनाधीयीत प्रतिषिद्धोऽस्य यज्ञः ।\nनित्योत्थितो भूतयेऽतन्द्रितः स्या-\nदेष स्मृतः शूद्रधर्मः पुराणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Serving and revering Brahmins is the duty of the Shudra, who is forbidden to study or sacrifice; he should always rise and be untiring for prosperity; this is remembered as the ancient Shudra duty."}},{"n":25,"text":"एतान्राजा पालयन्नप्रमत्तो\nनियोजयन्सर्ववर्णान्स्वधर्मे ।\nअकामात्मा समवृत्तिः प्रजासु\nनाधार्मिकाननुरुध्येत कामान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king, guarding these heedfully, keeping all classes in their own duty, without selfish desire, equal to the people, should not follow the desires of the unrighteous."}},{"n":26,"text":"श्रेयांस्तस्माद्यदि विद्येत कश्चि-\nदभिज्ञातः सर्वधर्मोपपन्नः ।\nस तं दुष्टमनुशिष्यात्प्रजान-\nन्न चेद्गृध्येदिति तस्मिन्न साधु ॥","meaning":{"en":"If there be someone better than him, known, endowed with all dharma, he should instruct that wicked one, knowing the people; if he is not greedy, it would not be good to attack him."}},{"n":27,"text":"यदा गृध्येत्परभूमिं नृशंसो\nविधिप्रकोपाद्बलमाददानः ।\nततो राज्ञां भविता युद्धमेत-\nत्तत्र जातं वर्म शस्त्रं धनुश्च ।\nइन्द्रेणेदं दस्युवधाय कर्म\nउत्पादितं वर्म शस्त्रं धनुश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a cruel one covets another's land, taking strength through violation of the rule, then war among kings will come; there armor, weapons and bow were born. Indra created this work to slay robbers: armor, weapon and bow."}},{"n":28,"text":"स्तेनो हरेद्यत्र धनं ह्यदृष्टः\nप्रसह्य वा यत्र हरेत दृष्टः ।\nउभौ गर्ह्यौ भवतः संजयैतौ\nकिं वै पृथक्त्वं धृतराष्ट्रस्य पुत्रे ।\nयोऽयं लोभान्मन्यते धर्ममेतं\nयमिच्छते मन्युवशानुगामी ॥","meaning":{"en":"A thief who takes wealth unseen, or one who takes it by force and is seen: both are blamed, Sanjaya; what difference is there with Dhritarashtra's son, who out of greed thinks this is dharma, which he wishes, following his anger?"}},{"n":29,"text":"भागः पुनः पाण्डवानां निविष्ट-\nस्तं नोऽकस्मादाददीरन्परे वै ।\nअस्मिन्पदे युध्यतां नो वधोऽपि\nश्लाघ्यः पित्र्यः परराज्याद्विशिष्टः ।\nएतान्धर्मान्कौरवाणां पुराणा-\nनाचक्षीथाः संजय राज्यमध्ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Moreover the Pandavas' share has been fixed; if others seized it from us without cause, then even death for us fighting here would be praised, traditional and better than another's kingdom. Tell these ancient duties of the Kauravas, Sanjaya, in the midst of the kingdom."}},{"n":30,"text":"ये ते मन्दा मृत्युवशाभिपन्नाः\nसमानीता धार्तराष्ट्रेण मूढाः ।\nइदं पुनः कर्म पापीय एव\nसभामध्ये पश्य वृत्तं कुरूणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These foolish ones who have fallen under death's control, brought together by Dhritarashtra's son, deluded: see again this very sinful deed, the conduct of the Kurus in the assembly."}},{"n":31,"text":"प्रियां भार्यां द्रौपदीं पाण्डवानां\nयशस्विनीं शीलवृत्तोपपन्नाम् ।\nयदुपेक्षन्त कुरवो भीष्ममुख्याः\nकामानुगेनोपरुद्धां रुदन्तीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The beloved wife of the Pandavas, Draupadi, famed, endowed with virtue and conduct, was neglected by the Kurus led by Bhishma while she wept, held by one following his lust."}},{"n":32,"text":"तं चेत्तदा ते सकुमारवृद्धा\nअवारयिष्यन्कुरवः समेताः ।\nमम प्रियं धृतराष्ट्रोऽकरिष्य-\nत्पुत्राणां च कृतमस्याभविष्यत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If the Kurus, young and old, had together stopped him then, Dhritarashtra would have done what I like, and what was good for his sons would have been done."}},{"n":33,"text":"दुःशासनः प्रातिलोम्यान्निनाय\nसभामध्ये श्वशुराणां च कृष्णाम् ।\nसा तत्र नीता करुणान्यवोच-\nन्नान्यं क्षत्तुर्नाथमदृष्ट कंचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duhshasana, perversely, led Krishna into the midst of the assembly, before her fathers-in-law; led there, she spoke piteously, and saw no other protector but Kshattri."}},{"n":34,"text":"कार्पण्यादेव सहितास्तत्र राज्ञो\nनाशक्नुवन्प्रतिवक्तुं सभायाम् ।\nएकः क्षत्ता धर्म्यमर्थं ब्रुवाणो\nधर्मं बुद्ध्वा प्रत्युवाचाल्पबुद्धिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Out of mere weakness the kings assembled there could not answer in the assembly; Kshattri alone, speaking what was proper for dharma and wealth, knowing dharma, answered the small-minded one."}},{"n":35,"text":"अनुक्त्वा त्वं धर्ममेवं सभाया-\nमथेच्छसे पाण्डवस्योपदेष्टुम् ।\nकृष्णा त्वेतत्कर्म चकार शुद्धं\nसुदुष्करं तद्धि सभां समेत्य ।\nयेन कृच्छ्रात्पाण्डवानुज्जहार\nतथात्मानं नौरिव सागरौघात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without speaking of dharma in that way in the assembly, you now wish to instruct the Pandava; but Krishna did that pure and very hard deed, having come to the assembly, by which she lifted the Pandavas out of hardship, as a boat takes one from a flood of the sea."}},{"n":36,"text":"यत्राब्रवीत्सूतपुत्रः सभायां\nकृष्णां स्थितां श्वशुराणां समीपे ।\nन ते गतिर्विद्यते याज्ञसेनि\nप्रपद्येदानीं धार्तराष्ट्रस्य वेश्म ।\nपराजितास्ते पतयो न सन्ति\nपतिं चान्यं भामिनि त्वं वृणीष्व ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where the charioteer's son, in the assembly, said to Krishna standing near her fathers-in-law: Daughter of Yajnasena, you have no way out; now enter Dhritarashtra's son's house; your husbands are defeated and are no more; choose another husband, lovely one."}},{"n":37,"text":"यो बीभत्सोर्हृदये प्रौढ आसी-\nदस्थिप्रच्छिन्मर्मघाती सुघोरः ।\nकर्णाच्छरो वाङ्मयस्तिग्मतेजाः\nप्रतिष्ठितो हृदये फल्गुनस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"That arrow-like speech of Karna, very terrible, striking the vitals, splitting bones, sharp in force, which had stood fixed in Bibhatsu's heart, remained lodged in Phalguna's heart."}},{"n":38,"text":"कृष्णाजिनानि परिधित्समाना-\nन्दुःशासनः कटुकान्यभ्यभाषत् ।\nएते सर्वे षण्ढतिला विनष्टाः\nक्षयं गता नरकं दीर्घकालम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duhshasana spoke harsh words to those who were putting on black deerskins: All these are barren sesame seeds, ruined, gone to destruction, to hell for a long time."}},{"n":39,"text":"गान्धारराजः शकुनिर्निकृत्या\nयदब्रवीद्द्यूतकाले स पार्थान् ।\nपराजितो नकुलः किं तवास्ति\nकृष्णया त्वं दीव्य वै याज्ञसेन्या ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni, king of Gandhara, by deceit, what he said to the Parthas at the time of the dice: Nakula is lost; what have you left? Play with Krishna, the daughter of Yajnasena."}},{"n":40,"text":"जानासि त्वं संजय सर्वमेत-\nद्द्यूतेऽवाच्यं वाक्यमेवं यथोक्तम् ।\nस्वयं त्वहं प्रार्थये तत्र गन्तुं\nसमाधातुं कार्यमेतद्विपन्नम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You know all this, Sanjaya, such unspeakable speech at the dice as it was said. I myself wish to go there to settle this broken matter."}},{"n":41,"text":"अहापयित्वा यदि पाण्डवार्थं\nशमं कुरूणामथ चेच्चरेयम् ।\nपुण्यं च मे स्याच्चरितं महोदयं\nमुच्येरंश्च कुरवो मृत्युपाशात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If, without neglecting the Pandavas' cause, I could bring peace for the Kurus, my action would be meritorious and bring great prosperity, and the Kurus would be freed from the noose of death."}},{"n":42,"text":"अपि वाचं भाषमाणस्य काव्यां\nधर्मारामामर्थवतीमहिंस्राम् ।\nअवेक्षेरन्धार्तराष्ट्राः समक्षं\nमां च प्राप्तं कुरवः पूजयेयुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And if Dhritarashtra's sons would give heed, in my presence, as I speak words that are wise, based on dharma, purposeful and non-violent, and the Kurus would honor me when I arrive,"}},{"n":43,"text":"अतोऽन्यथा रथिना फल्गुनेन\nभीमेन चैवाहवदंशितेन ।\nपरासिक्तान्धार्तराष्ट्रांस्तु विद्धि\nप्रदह्यमानान्कर्मणा स्वेन मन्दान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"but otherwise, understand that Dhritarashtra's sons will be struck down by the chariot-warrior Phalguna and by Bhima armored for battle, foolish ones burned by their own deeds."}},{"n":44,"text":"पराजितान्पाण्डवेयांस्तु वाचो\nरौद्ररूपा भाषते धार्तराष्ट्रः ।\nगदाहस्तो भीमसेनोऽप्रमत्तो\nदुर्योधनं स्मारयित्वा हि काले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra's son speaks terrible words to the defeated Pandavas; but Bhimasena, mace in hand, heedful, will in time remind Duryodhana."}},{"n":45,"text":"सुयोधनो मन्युमयो महाद्रुमः\nस्कन्धः कर्णः शकुनिस्तस्य शाखाः ।\nदुःशासनः पुष्पफले समृद्धे\nमूलं राजा धृतराष्ट्रोऽमनीषी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Suyodhana is a great tree of anger; Karna is its trunk, Shakuni its branches, Duhshasana its abundant flowers and fruits, and the king Dhritarashtra, unwise, its root."}},{"n":46,"text":"युधिष्ठिरो धर्ममयो महाद्रुमः\nस्कन्धोऽर्जुनो भीमसेनोऽस्य शाखाः ।\nमाद्रीपुत्रौ पुष्पफले समृद्धे\nमूलं त्वहं ब्रह्म च ब्राह्मणाश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira is a great tree of dharma; Arjuna is its trunk, Bhimasena its branches, the sons of Madri its abundant flowers and fruit, and I, with the Veda and the Brahmins, its root."}},{"n":47,"text":"वनं राजा धृतराष्ट्रः सपुत्रो\nव्याघ्रा वने संजय पाण्डवेयाः ।\nमा वनं छिन्धि सव्याघ्रं मा व्याघ्रान्नीनशो वनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Dhritarashtra with his sons is the forest, and the Pandavas, Sanjaya, are the tigers in the forest. Do not cut down the forest with its tigers, and do not lose the tigers from the forest."}},{"n":48,"text":"निर्वनो वध्यते व्याघ्रो निर्व्याघ्रं छिद्यते वनम् ।\nतस्माद्व्याघ्रो वनं रक्षेद्वनं व्याघ्रं च पालयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A forest without tigers is cut down, and tigers without a forest are killed; so let the tiger guard the forest, and let the forest protect the tiger."}},{"n":49,"text":"लताधर्मा धार्तराष्ट्राः शालाः संजय पाण्डवाः ।\nन लता वर्धते जातु अनाश्रित्य महाद्रुमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra's sons are the vines, Sanjaya, and the Pandavas are the sal trees; a vine never grows without the support of a great tree."}},{"n":50,"text":"स्थिताः शुश्रूषितुं पार्थाः स्थिता योद्धुमरिंदमाः ।\nयत्कृत्यं धृतराष्ट्रस्य तत्करोतु नराधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Parthas stand ready to serve and ready to fight, tamers of foes; let the king do whatever is the duty of Dhritarashtra."}},{"n":51,"text":"स्थिताः शमे महात्मानः पाण्डवा धर्मचारिणः ।\nयोधाः समृद्धास्तद्विद्वन्नाचक्षीथा यथातथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-souled Pandavas, who follow dharma, are set on peace; their warriors are prosperous; knowing this, wise one, report it just as it is."}}]}]}